Purchase Transaction – HP Printers
Given: Purchase 25 HP Printers @ ₹28,000 each + 18% GST. 4 printers are defective and 
returned. Pay 30% of the non-defective products.
A. Create Purchase Order
1. Open Tally Prime and select the required company. 
2. Go to Gateway of Tally → Vouchers. 
3. Select Purchase Order using Ctrl + F9. 
4. Select the supplier HP Technologies India Pvt Ltd. 
5. Enter the Order Number/Reference Number as DL005. 
6. Select the stock item HP Printer. 
7. Enter quantity as 25 Pieces. 
8. Enter the rate as ₹28,000 per Piece. 
9. Select/verify the appropriate CGST and SGST ledgers at 9% each. 
10. Check the order value and GST amount. 
11. Accept and save the Purchase Order. 
B. Create Purchase Voucher
12. Go to Gateway of Tally → Vouchers → Purchase (F9). 
13. Select HP Technologies India Pvt Ltd as the party. 
14. Use Agst Ref/Order and select the previously created Purchase Order. 
15. Enter 25 Pieces of HP Printer at ₹28,000. 
16. Verify that 18% GST is calculated correctly. 
17. Enter/select the appropriate purchase ledger. 
18. Verify the total invoice amount. 
19. Accept and save the Purchase Voucher. 
20. In Bill-wise Details, select New Ref and enter the invoice/reference details as required. 
C. Return 4 Defective Printers – Debit Note
21. Go to Gateway of Tally → Vouchers. 
22. Select Debit Note using Ctrl + F9. 
23. Select HP Technologies India Pvt Ltd as the party. 
24. Select/reference the original purchase invoice. 
25. Enter 4 Pieces of HP Printer. 
26. Enter the rate as ₹28,000 per Piece. 
27. Verify the applicable 18% GST reversal/adjustment. 
28. Check the debit note value. 
29. Accept and save the Debit Note. 
30. Verify that the stock quantity has been reduced by 4 Printers. 
D. Make 30% Payment 31. Calculate the value of the 21 non-defective printers. 
32. Calculate 30% of the amount payable after considering the purchase return. 
33. Go to Gateway of Tally → Vouchers → Payment (F5). 
34. Select the appropriate Bank/Cash Ledger. 
35. Select HP Technologies India Pvt Ltd as the party. 
36. Use Bill-wise Details → Agst Ref and select the outstanding purchase bill. 
37. Enter the calculated 30% payment amount. 
38. Verify the remaining outstanding balance. 
39. Accept and save the Payment Voucher. 
2. Sales Transaction – HP Printers
Given: Sell 18 HP Printers @ ₹35,000 each + 18% GST. 5 are returned. Receive 40% payment 
for the non-defective products.
A. Create Sales Order
1. Open Tally Prime and select the required company. 
2. Go to Gateway of Tally → Vouchers. 
3. Select Sales Order using Ctrl + F8. 
4. Select Eatence Technologies India Pvt Ltd as the customer. 
5. Enter the Order Number/Reference Number as EL005. 
6. Select the stock item HP Printer. 
7. Enter quantity as 18 Pieces. 
8. Enter the rate as ₹35,000 per Piece. 
9. Select the appropriate CGST and SGST ledgers at 9% each. 
10. Verify the GST and total order value. 
11. Accept and save the Sales Order. 
B. Create Sales Voucher
12. Go to Gateway of Tally → Vouchers → Sales (F8). 
13. Select Eatence Technologies India Pvt Ltd as the party. 
14. Use Agst Ref/Order and select the previously created Sales Order. 
15. Enter 18 Pieces of HP Printer at ₹35,000. 
16. Verify the applicable 18% GST. 
17. Select the appropriate sales ledger. 
18. Verify the invoice total. 
19. Accept and save the Sales Voucher. 
20. Enter the appropriate Bill-wise Reference Details. 
C. Return 5 Printers – Credit Note 21. Go to Gateway of Tally → Vouchers. 
22. Select Credit Note using Alt + F8. 
23. Select Eatence Technologies India Pvt Ltd as the party. 
24. Reference the original sales invoice. 
25. Enter 5 Pieces of HP Printer. 
26. Enter the rate as ₹35,000 per Piece. 
27. Verify the applicable 18% GST adjustment. 
28. Check the credit note value. 
29. Accept and save the Credit Note. 
30. Verify that the 5 returned Printers are added back to stock. 
D. Receive 40% Payment
31. Calculate the value of the 13 non-defective printers. 
32. Calculate 40% of the amount receivable for the non-defective products. 
33. Go to Gateway of Tally → Vouchers → Receipt (F6). 
34. Select the appropriate Bank/Cash Ledger. 
35. Select Eatence Technologies India Pvt Ltd as the party. 
36. Select Agst Ref under Bill-wise Details. 
37. Select the outstanding sales invoice. 
38. Enter the calculated 40% receipt amount. 
39. Verify the remaining receivable amount. 
40. Accept and save the Receipt Voucher. 
3. Purchase Return Transaction – HP 
Printers
Given: Purchase 32 HP Printers @ ₹30,000 each + 18% GST. 6 are defective and returned. Pay 
50% of the remaining non-defective products.
A. Create Purchase Order
1. Open Tally Prime and select the required company. 
2. Go to Gateway of Tally → Vouchers. 
3. Select Purchase Order (Ctrl + F9). 
4. Select HP Technologies India Pvt Ltd as the supplier. 
5. Enter the reference/invoice number as DL006. 
6. Select HP Printer as the stock item. 
7. Enter quantity as 32 Pieces. 
8. Enter rate as ₹30,000 per Piece. 
9. Apply 18% GST. 
10. Verify the order value and GST calculation. 11. Accept and save the Purchase Order. 
B. Create Purchase Voucher
12. Open Purchase Voucher (F9). 
13. Select HP Technologies India Pvt Ltd. 
14. Select the previously created Purchase Order using the appropriate reference option. 
15. Enter/verify 32 Pieces at ₹30,000. 
16. Verify the 18% GST calculation. 
17. Select the appropriate purchase ledger. 
18. Check the invoice total. 
19. Enter the required Bill-wise Reference Details. 
20. Accept and save the Purchase Voucher. 
C. Return 6 Defective Printers
21. Open Debit Note (Ctrl + F9). 
22. Select HP Technologies India Pvt Ltd. 
23. Reference the original purchase invoice. 
24. Select HP Printer. 
25. Enter quantity as 6 Pieces. 
26. Enter the rate as ₹30,000 per Piece. 
27. Verify the applicable 18% GST adjustment. 
28. Verify the debit note amount. 
29. Accept and save the Debit Note. 
30. Check the stock position to ensure the 6 returned Printers are deducted. 
D. Make 50% Payment
31. Calculate the number of non-defective Printers: 32 − 6 = 26 Pieces. 
32. Calculate the value of the 26 non-defective Printers. 
33. Calculate 50% of the payable amount. 
34. Open Payment Voucher (F5). 
35. Select the appropriate Bank/Cash Ledger. 
36. Select HP Technologies India Pvt Ltd. 
37. Select Agst Ref under Bill-wise Details. 
38. Select the outstanding purchase invoice. 
39. Enter the calculated 50% payment amount. 
40. Verify the remaining outstanding amount. 
41. Accept and save the Payment Voucher.
